This may be true for {soi}, but I'm not at all sure it's true for {xoi}.=20
There are two options for {xoi}: it's either restrictive or=20
non-restrictive. If it is one of the two, then we don't have a word for=20
the other and vice versa. There should really be two {xoi}. Let's call=20
them {Pxoi} and {Nxoi}. There is an important difference between (E) and=20
(F):

    (E) so'i verba cu krixa Pxoi fanza
        "Many children are yelling annoyingly."
        (There may be children there whose yelling isn't annoying)

    (F) so'i verba cu krixa Nxoi fanza
        "Many children are yelling, which is annoying."
        (Every yelling child is annoying)

Which one is {xoi} supposed to be?

